  "title": "Night & Day of 25th Zilqad (The Spreading of the earth)",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "THE TWENTY-FIFTH NIGHT OF ZILQAD (The Earth Spreading night)\nThis night is called laylat dahw al-arz (the night at which the earth was spread on the water where the Holy Ka’bah is now situated). Being distinctively honorable, at this night the mercy of Almighty Allah is poured on people. A great reward is obtained by those who practice acts of worship at this night. Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Washsha’ has narrated that when he was young, he was with his father in the hospitality of Imam al-Reza (a.s.) at the twenty-fifth night of Dhu’l-Qa’dah. After they had their supper, Imam al-Reza (a.s.) said, “At the twenty-fifth night of Dhu’l-Qa’dah, Prophet Ibrahim (a.s.) was born, Prophet Eesaa (a.s.) the son of Mary was born, and the earth was spread on the water where the Holy Ka’bah is now situated. Hence, if one observes fasting on this day, he will be given the reward of observing fasting in sixth months.” According to another narration, Imam al-Reza (a.s.) added, “Verily, on this day, al-Qa’im (i.e. Imam al-Mahdi) (a.t.f.s.) will appear.”\nTHE TWENTY-FIFTH OF ZILQAD (The Earth Spreading Day)\nThe twenty-fifth of Zilqad is one of the four days on which fasting is exclusively confirmed. According to a narration, to observe fasting on this day is equal to seventy year fasting. It also erases the sins of seventy years. According to another narration, to observe fasting on this day and to practice acts of worship at its night is equal (in reward) to one hundred year worship. Everything that is between the sky and the earth will ask God’s forgiveness for one who does these rites. On this day, the mercy of Almighty Allah has been spread. To practice acts of worship and hold sessions for mentioning Almighty Allah on this day bring about an abundant reward. Apart from fasting, acts of worship, remembrance of Almighty Allah, and bathing, there are two other acts that are advisably done on this day:\nFirst: The books written by Shi’ite scholars of Qumm have mentioned that, on this day, it is recommended to offer, in the morning, a prayer consisting of two units, reciting in the each unit [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and repeating [Surah al-Shams](A95) (No. 91) five times. After accomplishment, the following litany is said:\nلَا حَوْلَ وَ لَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nLAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A’LIYYIL A’ZEEMO\nThere is no power and no strength except with Allah, the Most High, the All-great.\nThen, one may pray Almighty Allah for granting his needs and then say the following supplicatory prayer:\nيَا مُقِيْلَ الْعَثَرَاتِ اَقِلْنِيْ عَثْرَتِيْ\nYAA MOQEELAL A’SARAATE AQILNEE A’SRATEE\nO He Who overlooks slips, (please) overlook my slip. \nيَا مُجِيْبَ الدَّعَوَاتِ اَجِبْ دَعْوَتِيْ\nYAA MOJEEBAD DA-A’WAATE AJIB DA’WATEE\nO He Who responds to prayers, (please) respond to my prayer. \nيَا سَامِعَ الْاَصْوَاتِ اسْمَعْ صَوْتِيْ\nYAA SAAME-A’L ASWAATIS MA’ SAWTEE\nO He Who hears all sounds, (please) listen to mine, \nوَ ارْحَمْنِيْ وَ تَجَاوَزْ عَنْ سَيِّئَاتِيْ\nWAR HAMNEE WA TAJAAWAZ A’N SAYYE-AATEE\nhave mercy on me, and excuse my wrongdoings \nوَ مَا عِنْدِيْ يَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَ الْاِكْرَامِ.\nWA MAA I’NDEE YAA ZAL JALAALE WAL IKRAAME.\nand whatever I have committed. O Lord of majesty and honor!\nSecond: In Misbah al-Mutahajjid, Shaykh al-Tusi has mentioned that it is recommended to say the following supplicatory prayer on this day:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ دَاحِيَ الْكَعْبَةِ وَ فَالِقَ الْحَبَّةِ\nALLAAHUMMA DAAHE-YAL KA’BATE WA FAALEQAL HABBATE\nO Allah Who spread the Ka'bah, split the kernel, \nوَ صَارِفَ اللَّزْبَةِ وَ كَاشِفَ كُلِّ كُرْبَةٍ\nWA SAAREFAL LAZBATE WA KAASHEFA KULLE KURBATIN\nremoves troubles, and relieves from all distresses! \nاَسْاَلُكَ فِىْ هٰذَا الْيَوْمِ مِنْ اَيَّامِكَ\nAS-ALOKA FEE HAAZAL YAWME MIN AYYAAMEKAL\nI beseech You on this day, which is one of Your days \nالَّتِيْ اَعْظَمْتَ حَقَّهَا وَ اَقْدَمْتَ سَبْقَهَا\nLATEE A-A’ZAMTA HAQQAHAA WA AQDAMTA SABQAHAA\nwhose standing You have deemed great, whom You have given preference, \nوَ جَعَلْتَهَا عِنْدَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَدِيْعَةً\nWA JA-A’LTAHAA I’NDAL MOAMENEENA WADEE-A’TAN\nand whom You have put as trust with the believers \nوَ اِلَيْكَ ذَرِيْعَةً وَ بِرَحْمَتِكَ الْوَسِيْعَةِ\nWA ELAYKA ZAREE-A’TAN WA BE-RAHMATEKAL WASEE-A’TE\nand as means to approaching to You; and [I beseech You] in the name of Your ample mercy \nاَنْ تُصَلِّىَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ عَبْدِكَ الْمُنْتَجَبِ\nAN TOSALLEYA A’LAA MOHAMMADIN A’BDEKAL MUNTAJABE\nto send blessings to Muhammad, Your servant that You have selected \nفِي الْمِيْثَاقِ الْقَرِيْبِ يَوْمَ التَّلَاقِ\nFIL MEESAAQIL QAREEBE YAWMAT TALAAQE\nin the Nigh Covenant on the Meeting Day, \nفَاتِقِ كُلِّ رَتْقٍ وَ دَاعٍ اِلٰى كُلِّ حَقٍّ\nFAATEQE KULLE RATQIN WA DAA-IN ELAA KULLE HAQQIN\nthe splitter of all joined things and the caller to all truths, \nوَ عَلٰىۤ اَهْلِ بَيْتِهِ الْاَطْهَارِ\nWA A’LAA AHLE BAYTEHIL ATHAARIL\nand to his Household, the pure, \nالْهُدَاةِ الْمَنَارِ دَعَاۤئِمِ الْجَبَّارِ\nHODAATIL MANAARE DA-A’AA-EMIL JABBAARE\nthe guides, the lanterns, the pillars of the Omnipotent (Lord), \nوَ وُلَاةِ الْجَنَّةِ وَ النَّارِ\nWA WOLAATIL JANNATE WAN NAARE\nand the supervisors on Paradise and Hell, \nوَ اَعْطِنَا فِيْ يَوْمِنَا هٰذَا\nWA A-A’TENAA FEE YAWMENAA HAAZAA\nto give us on this day \nمِنْ عَطَاۤئِكَ الْمَخْزُوْنِ\nMIN A’TAA-EKAL MAKHZOONE\nfrom Your stored gifts, \nغَيْرَ مَقْطُوْعٍ وَ لَا مَمْنُوْعٍ\nGHAYRA MAQTOO-I’N WA LAA MAMNOO-I’N\ngifts that are neither interrupted nor prohibited \nتَجْمَعُ لَنَا بِهِ التَّوْبَةَ وَ حُسْنَ الْاَوْبَةِ\nTAJ-MA-O’ LANAA BEHIT TAWBATA WA HUSNAL AWBATE\nby which You join for us both repentance and acceptable return [to You]. \nيَا خَيْرَ مَدْعُوٍّ وَ اَكْرَمَ مَرْجُوٍّ\nYAA KHAYRA MAD-U’WWIN WA AKRAMA MARJUWWIN\nO He Who is the best of all supplicated ones and the most generous of all hoped ones! \nيَا كَفِيُّ يَا وَفِيُّ يَا مَنْ لُطْفُهٗ خَفِيٌّ\nYAA KAFIYYO YAA WAFIYYO YAA MAN LUTFOHU KHAFIYYUN\nO All-sufficer! O All-true! O He Whose grace is gentle! \nاُلْطُفْ لِيْ بِلُطْفِكَ وَ اَسْعِدْنِيْ بِعَفْوِكَ\nULTUF LEE BE-LUTFEKA WA AS-I’DNEE BE-A’FWEKA\n(Please) treat me gracefully with Your graciousness, make me feel happy with Your pardon, \nوَ اَيِّدْنِيْ بِنَصْرِكَ وَ لَا تُنْسِنِيْ كَرِيْمَ ذِكْرِكَ\nWA AYYIDNEE BE-NASREKA WA LAA TUNSENEE KAREEMA ZIKREKA\naid me with Your support, never make me inattentive of Your noble mention \nبِوُلَاةِ اَمْرِكَ وَ حَفَظَةِ سِرِّكَ\nBEWOLAATE AMREKA WA HAFAZATE SIRREKA\nthrough Your Representatives and the keepers of Your secret, \nوَ احْفَظْنِيْ مِنْ شَوَاۤئِبِ الدَّهْرِ\nWAH FAZNEE MIN SHAWAA-EBID DAHRE\nprotect me against the vicissitudes of time \nاِلٰى يَوْمِ الْحَشْرِ وَ النَّشْرِ\nELAA YAWMIL HASHRE WAN NASHRE\nup to the day of resurrection and raising (the dead to life), \nوَ اَشْهِدْنِيْۤ اَوْلِيَاۤئَكَ عِنْدَ خُرُوْجِ نَفْسِيْ\nWA ASH-HIDNEE AWLEYAA-AKA I’NDA KHOROOJE NAFSEE\nand make Your Representatives attend at the hour of the departure of my souls, \nوَ حُلُوْلِ رَمْسِيْ وَ انْقِطَاعِ عَمَلِيْ وَ انْقِضَاۤءِ اَجَلِيْۤ\nWA HOLOOLE RAMSEE WAN QETAA-E’ A’MALEE WAN QEZAAA-E AJALEE\nthe time of my entry to my grave, when my deed will be interrupted and my lifetime will come to its end. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَ اذْكُرْنِيْ عَلٰى طُوْلِ الْبِلٰىۤ\nALLAAHUMMA WAZ KURNEE A’LAA TOOLIL BALAA\nO Allah, (please) remember me all over the stages of trial \nاِذَا حَلَلْتُ بَيْنَ اَطْبَاقِ الثَّرٰى\nEZAA HALALTO BAYNA ATBAAQIS SARAA\nwhen I will reside between the layers of the earth \nوَ نَسِيَنِيَ النَّاسُوْنَ مِنَ الْوَرٰى\nWA NASEYANEYAN NAASOONA MENAL WARAA\nand the forgetful people will forget me. \nوَ اَحْلِلْنِيْ دَارَ الْمُقَامَةِ\nWA AHLILNEE DAARAL MOQAAMATE\nAllow me to dwell in the abode of eternity, \nوَ بَوِّئْنِيْ مَنْزِلَ الْكَرَامَةِ،\nWA BAWWEANEE MANZELAL KARAAMATE\nsettle me in the residence of honor, \nوَ اجْعَلْنِىْ مِنْ مُرَافِقِيْ اَوْلِيَاۤئِكَ\nWAJ A’LNEE MIN MORAAFEQEE AWLEYAAA-EKA\nmake me of the companions of Your intimate servants \nوَ اَهْلِ اجْتِبَاۤئِكَ وَ اصْطِفَاۤئِكَ\nWA AHLIJ TEBAA-EKA WAS TEFAA-EKA\nand the people of Your choice and selection, \nوَ بَارِكْ لِيْ فِيْ لِقَاۤئِكَ\nWA BAARIK LEE FEE LEQAAA-EKA\nbless me by meeting You, \nوَ ارْزُقْنِيْ حُسْنَ الْعَمَلِ\nWAR ZUQNEEHUSNAL A’MALE\nand grant me good doing \nقَبْلَ حُلُوْلِ الْاَجَلِ\nQABLA HOLOOLIL AJALE\nbefore the end of my lifetime, \nبَرِيْئًا مِنَ الزَّلَلِ وَ سُوْۤءِ الْخَطَلِ\nBAREE-AN MENAZ ZALALE WA SOOIL KHATALE\nmaking me free from slips and foolish doing. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَ اَوْرِدْنِىْ حَوْضَ نَبِيِّكَ\nALLAAHUMMA WA AWRIDNEE HAWZA NABIYYEKA\nO Allah, allow me to enter the Pool of Your Prophet, \nمُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ اٰلِهٖ\nMOHAMMADIN SALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WAA AALEHI\nMuhammad, Allah’s blessings be upon him and his Household, \nوَ اسْقِنِيْ مِنْهُ مَشْرَبًا\nWAS QENEE MINHO MASHRABAN\nallow me to drink from it a quenching drink \nرَوِيًّا سَاۤئِغًا هَنِيْۤئًا\nRAWIYYAN SAA-EGHAN HANEE-AN\nthat is palatable and salubrious \nلَاۤ اَظْمَاُ بَعْدَهٗ وَ لَاۤ اَحْلَاُ وِرْدَهٗ\nLAA AZMA-O BA’DAHU WA LAA AHALA-O WIRDAHU\nafter which I will never be thirsty, I will never be prevented from reaching it, \nوَ لَا عَنْهُ اُذَادُ وَ اجْعَلْهُ لِيْ خَيْرَ زَادٍ\nWA LAA A’NHO OZAADO WAJ A’LHO LEE KHAYRA ZAADIN\nand I will never be disallowed to approach it. Make for me the best nourishment \nوَ اَوْفٰى مِيْعَادٍ يَوْمَ يَقُوْمُ الْاَشْهَادُ\nWA AWFAA MEE-A’ADIN YAWMA YAQOOMUL ASH-HAADO\nand the most fulfilling promise on the day when the Witnesses will rise. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَ الْعَنْ جَبَابِرَةَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَ الْاٰخِرِيْنَ\nALLAAHUMMA WAL A’N JABAABERATAL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHEREENA\nO Allah, curse the tyrants from the past and the last generations \nوَ بِحُقُوْقِ اَوْلِيَاۤئِكَ الْمُسْتَأْثِرِيْنَ\nWA BE-HOQOOQE AWLEYAA-EKAL MUSTAA-SEREENA\nwho usurped the dues of Your Representatives. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَ اقْصِمْ دَعَاۤئِمَهُمْ\nALLAAHUMMA WAQ SIM DA-A’AEMAHUM\nO Allah, demolish their posts, \nوَ اَهْلِكْ اَشْيَاعَهُمْ وَ عَامِلَهُمْ\nWA AHLIK ASHYAA-A’HUM WA A’AMELAHUM\nannihilate their allies and their assistants, \nوَ عَجِّلْ مَهَالِكَهُمْ وَ اسْلُبْهُمْ مَمَالِكَهُمْ\nWA A’JJIL MAHAALEKAHUM WAS LUBHUM MAMAALEKAHUM\nand hasten their perdition, seize their estates, \nوَ ضَيِّقْ عَلَيْهِمْ مَسَالِكَهُمْ\nWA ZAYYIQ A’LAYHIM MASAALEKAHUM\nmake narrow their ways, \nوَ الْعَنْ مُسَاهِمَهُمْ وَ مُشَارِكَهُمْ.\nWAL A’N MOSAAHEMAHUM WA MOSHAAREKAHUM.\nand curse their helpers and aides. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَ عَجِّلْ فَرَجَ اَوْلِيَاۤئِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA WA A’JJIL FARAJA AWLEYAA-EKA\nAllah, (please) hasten the relief of Your Representatives, \nوَ ارْدُدْ عَلَيْهِمْ مَظَالِمَهُمْ\nWAR DUD A’LAYHIM MAZAAEMAHUM\nrestore to them their usurped rights, \nوَ اَظْهِرْ بِالْحَقِّ قَاۤئِمَهُمْ\nWA AZHIR BIL HAQQE QAA-EMAHUM\ncause their Riser to prevail with the truth, \nوَ اجْعَلْهُ لِدِيْنِكَ مُنْتَصِرًا\nWAJ-A’LHO LEDEENEKA MUNTASERAN\nand make him support Your religion \nوَ بِاَمْرِكَ فِيْۤ اَعْدَاۤئِكَ مُؤْتَمِرًا\nWA BE-AMREKA FEE A-A’DAA-EKA MOATAMERAN\nand carry out Your commandments about Your enemies. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ احْفُفْهُ بِمَلَاۤئِكَةِ النَّصْرِ\nALLAAHUMMAH FUFHO BEMALAA-EKATIN NASRE\nO Allah, make the angels of victory surround him \nوَ بِمَاۤ اَلْقَيْتَ اِلَيْهِ مِنَ الْاَمْرِ\nWA BEMAA ALQAYTA ELAYHE MENAL AMRE\nand so are the commandments that You addressed to him \nفِيْ لَيْلَةِ الْقَدْرِ مُنْتَقِمًا لَكَ\nFEE LAYLATIL QADRE MUNTAQEMAN LAKA\nat the Destiny Night so that he will punish Your enemies on behalf of You \nحَتّٰى تَرْضٰى وَ يَعُوْدَ دِيْنُكَ بِهٖ\nHATTAA TARZAA WA YA-O’ODA DEENOKA BEHI\nuntil You are pleased, Your religion will recover \nوَ عَلٰى يَدَيْهِ جَدِيْدًا غَضًّا\nWA A’LAA YADAYHE JADEEDAN GHAZZAN\nits freshness and bloom at his hands, \nوَ يَمْحَضَ الْحَقَّ مَحْضًا وَ يَرْفِضَ الْبَاطِلَ رَفْضًا\nWA YAMHAZAL HAQQA MAHZAN WA YARFEZAL BAATELA RAFZAN\nhe will clean the truth with thorough cleaning, and he will reject the wrong with absolute rejection. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَيْهِ وَ عَلٰى جَمِيْعِ اٰبَاۤئِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAYHE WA A’LAA JAMEE-E’ AABAAA-EHI\nO Allah, send blessings to him and to all of his forefathers, \nوَ اجْعَلْنَا مِنْ صَحْبِهٖ وَ اُسْرَتِهٖ\nWAJ A’LNAA MIN SAHBEHI WA USRATEHI\ninclude us with his companions and group, \nوَ ابْعَثْنَا فِيْ كَرَّتِهٖ حَتّٰى نَكُوْنَ فِيْ زَمَانِهٖ مِنْ اَعْوَانِهٖ\nWAB A’SNAA FEE KARRATEHI HATTAA NAKOONA FEE ZAMAANEHI MIN A-A’WAANEHI\nand resurrect us during his return (raj’at) so that we will live in his age and become of his helpers. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَدْرِكْ بِنَا قِيَامَهٗ\nALLAAHUMMA ADRIK BENAA QEYAAMAHU\nO Allah, make us catch up his advent, \nوَ اَشْهِدْنَا اَيَّامَهٗ وَ صَلِّ عَلَيْهِ [عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ]\nWA ASHIDNAA AYYAAMAHU WA SALLE A’LAYHE (A’LAA MOHAMMADIN)\nmake us witness his days, bless him, \nوَ ارْدُدْ اِلَيْنَا سَلَامَهٗ\nWAR DUD ELAYNAA SALAAMAHU\nand convey to us his greetings. \nوَ السَّلَامُ عَلَيْهِ [عَلَيْهِمْ‏] وَ رَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَ بَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWAS SALAAMO A’LAYHE (A’LAYHIM) WA RAHMATUL LAAHE WA BARAKAATOHU.\nPeace and Allah’s mercy and blessings be upon him.\nIn his epistle entitled al-Arba’at Ayyam (The Four Days), Sayyid al-Damad has mentioned that to visit the holy tomb of Imam Ali ibn Musa al-Reza (a.s.) on the day; i.e. the Earth Spreading Day, is the most preferable act. Similarly, to visit his tomb on the first of Rajab is highly desirable; therefore, he has urged on it greatly."
}
